From 742f33436321b00745684ba4c41667a5e9004bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Guise <aaron@guise.net.nz>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:31:24 +1200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] build(docker): drop stalwart-cli from the shipped image,
 enable rocks via a newer cross image

stalwart-cli isn't used by this deployment - stop building and shipping
it. Cross-compiling librocksdb-sys needs a newer libclang than the
default 'cross' images carry (Ubuntu 16.04 / libclang 3.8); pin the
':main'-tagged images instead (Cross.toml, Ubuntu 24.04 / libclang 19,
matching what the official Dockerfile installs), which lets 'rocks'
build cleanly and replace the sqlite/postgres/mysql/elastic mix with
sqlite/postgres/mysql/rocks. depot.json pins the Depot build project
used for remote/cached cross-compilation.
---
 .dockerignore   |  23 ++++++++
 Cross.toml      |  17 ++++++
 Dockerfile.fast |  35 ++++++++++++
 Justfile        | 149 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 README.md       |  39 +++++++++++++
 build.sh        | 118 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
